1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Last time, you learned to set the odds.

2
00:00:04,378 --> 00:00:08,726
How many systems have enemies, how big the fleets are,

3
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:10,915
how close they wait.

4
00:00:12,715 --> 00:00:17,498
But a story has one place where odds aren't good enough.

5
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:21,441
When the crew gets to the end,

6
00:00:21,891 --> 00:00:24,500
the fight has to be there.

7
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,343
Today you stage that one fight yourself.

8
00:00:30,543 --> 00:00:33,152
Here's the end of my story.

9
00:00:34,052 --> 00:00:38,400
It says four Gleaner hulls stand between you and them.

10
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,939
Well, do they really?

11
00:00:42,839 --> 00:00:47,622
Last time I counted four Gleaner ships at the Bone Pile.

12
00:00:48,522 --> 00:00:53,304
But they're only there because the game rolled an enemy system,

13
00:00:53,754 --> 00:00:56,363
and every new game rolls again.

14
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:02,076
I asked the game about four hundred new games,

15
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:09,048
and in about four of every ten the Bone Pile was not an enemy system.

16
00:01:09,948 --> 00:01:10,948
In those,

17
00:01:11,398 --> 00:01:16,180
the crew arrives for the last fight and finds three raiders.

18
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:19,120
So here's a card.

19
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:24,802
It's the only new piece of MAST in this whole class,

20
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:29,600
and you don't need to be able to write it.

21
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,109
You copy it from the page,

22
00:01:33,559 --> 00:01:37,037
to the very end of the story file.

23
00:01:38,837 --> 00:01:41,446
One of these lines is long.

24
00:01:42,346 --> 00:01:45,389
It's one line, so don't break it.

25
00:01:47,189 --> 00:01:50,233
Let's read it once, from the top.

26
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:54,611
The line with two slashes is a route.

27
00:01:55,511 --> 00:01:58,554
The game says, a ship has arrived,

28
00:01:59,004 --> 00:02:01,178
and this block hears it.

29
00:02:02,078 --> 00:02:06,426
The rest of that line says, only in this system.

30
00:02:08,226 --> 00:02:10,400
Then it waits one second.

31
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:16,517
Then it asks, is this step of the story open right now?

32
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:18,707
If not, it stops.

33
00:02:20,507 --> 00:02:22,246
And if it is,

34
00:02:22,696 --> 00:02:26,609
it finds where the system is, makes one fleet,

35
00:02:27,059 --> 00:02:29,667
and shows the crew a card.

36
00:02:30,867 --> 00:02:34,780
There are seven things you change, and nothing else.

37
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:39,189
The two numbers of the system,

38
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:42,248
which you copy from the landmark.

39
00:02:43,148 --> 00:02:46,191
The key of the step, in quotes.

40
00:02:47,091 --> 00:02:50,135
The kind of ship, and the tier,

41
00:02:50,585 --> 00:02:54,498
and you know both of those from last time.

42
00:02:55,398 --> 00:02:58,876
The key of the side they fight for,

43
00:02:59,326 --> 00:03:02,804
which has to come first inside those quotes.

44
00:03:03,704 --> 00:03:06,313
How far away they form up.

45
00:03:07,213 --> 00:03:09,822
And the sentence the crew reads.

46
00:03:11,022 --> 00:03:15,804
Two parts of this card look like details, and they aren't.

47
00:03:17,604 --> 00:03:20,213
The first is the word shared.

48
00:03:21,113 --> 00:03:25,896
A route without it runs once for every console that's connected.

49
00:03:26,796 --> 00:03:31,143
Anything that makes a ship goes on a shared route,

50
00:03:31,593 --> 00:03:34,637
or every console makes its own fleet.

51
00:03:36,437 --> 00:03:39,046
The second is the one-second wait.

52
00:03:39,946 --> 00:03:41,685
When the crew arrives,

53
00:03:42,135 --> 00:03:47,787
the game finishes one step and reveals the next, at that same moment.

54
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:52,165
Without the wait, my card looks too early.

55
00:03:52,615 --> 00:03:56,528
It sees a hidden step, and it makes nothing.

56
00:03:57,428 --> 00:04:02,646
I took that line out to check, and that's exactly what happened.

57
00:04:03,846 --> 00:04:06,454
So when is the battle there?

58
00:04:07,354 --> 00:04:09,093
I played every case.

59
00:04:10,893 --> 00:04:14,372
If the crew wanders in early, there's nothing,

60
00:04:14,822 --> 00:04:17,430
because the step is still hidden.

61
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:22,243
If they arrive on the story's business, it's there.

62
00:04:24,043 --> 00:04:29,261
If they run and come back, there's one battle line, not two,

63
00:04:29,711 --> 00:04:33,624
because the system is taken down when they leave.

64
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:37,133
After a Continue, it's there again.

65
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:41,511
And once the step is done, it's gone.

66
00:04:43,311 --> 00:04:45,050
There's one warning here.

67
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:49,863
The tier on the card doesn't move with Difficulty,

68
00:04:50,313 --> 00:04:54,226
so add it to your budget from last time.

69
00:04:55,126 --> 00:04:58,170
Mine comes to eleven or twelve ships,

70
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:01,663
which is a lot for one cruiser.

71
00:05:02,863 --> 00:05:06,341
Lint says clean, as it did last time.

72
00:05:07,241 --> 00:05:13,328
And once again, it can't see most of what goes wrong on this card,

73
00:05:13,778 --> 00:05:16,822
so use the list on the page.

74
00:05:18,622 --> 00:05:20,796
Now let's play the story.

75
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:24,739
The Tern first, and then the ledger.

76
00:05:25,189 --> 00:05:29,102
And then the place the Gleaners won't talk about.

77
00:05:30,902 --> 00:05:32,641
There are three cards.

78
00:05:33,091 --> 00:05:35,700
The place, the guards, and mine.

79
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,209
Now I'll run, and come back.

80
00:05:40,109 --> 00:05:42,283
There's still one battle line.

81
00:05:43,483 --> 00:05:45,222
Now it's your turn.

82
00:05:46,122 --> 00:05:52,209
Find the one place in your story where the fight has to be there.

83
00:05:53,109 --> 00:05:57,457
If you don't have one, you don't need this card.

84
00:05:59,257 --> 00:06:01,430
If you do, paste it,

85
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:06,663
change the seven words, and then go there early on purpose.

86
00:06:07,563 --> 00:06:09,737
There should be nothing waiting.

87
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:16,320
Next time, somebody else gets to play your universe, from above.
